<section id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-h">
  <h2 id="experience-h">Experience</h2>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-head">
      <h3>INKOMPASS Technical Service &amp; Production Intern</h3>
      <p class="meta">June 2025 – May 2026</p>
    </div>
    <p class="meta">Philip Morris International (PMI), Izmir, Turkey</p>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>Developed and supported Power BI dashboards that visualize critical production metrics, including machine efficiency, uptime and losses.</li>
      <li>Monitored real-time motor diagnostics (current, torque, temperature) in Grafana, working with the Global IT Team to troubleshoot data pipeline errors and resolve unresponsive metrics.</li>
      <li>Assisted in deploying and analyzing vibration sensor data on rotating equipment to build data-driven predictive maintenance schedules and minimize unscheduled downtime.</li>
      <li>Led a technical audit of plant pneumatic networks with an LD-500 ultrasonic leak detector, identifying and resolving air leaks and writing repair recommendation reports.</li>
      <li>Designed EHS training sessions and in-machine maintenance training modules, and presented daily Quality Flags and production efficiency reports.</li>
      <li>Analyzed conveyor belt speeds and stopper distances on high-speed industrial printers, reducing non-readable product rates in Track &amp; Trace (HERMOS) systems.</li>
      <li>Resolved network connectivity issues for industrial robots and optimized sensor performance inside robot cages to maximize uptime and MTBF.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-h">
  <h2 id="projects-h">Projects</h2>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-head">
      <h3>Industrial Control Panel &amp; PLC Systems</h3>
      <p class="meta">Summer 2026</p>
    </div>
    <p class="meta">Field practice, Industrial Zone, Izmir</p>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>Assembled and wired industrial electrical control panels using components from ABB, Schneider, Siemens, Chint and Hyundai, including contactors, thermal overload relays and circuit protection devices.</li>
      <li>Diagnosed and tested PLC units before replacement decisions, preventing unnecessary equipment purchases and reducing operational costs.</li>
      <li>Performed motor wiring, panel-to-motor connections and in-panel circuit board testing, and implemented star-delta motor starting logic in panel design.</li>
      <li>Worked with a senior electrical engineer to design, assemble and price a Siemens PLC-controlled panel with HMI for a dual-line temperature control system in a residential thermal water heating application.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-head">
      <h3>DeskBuddy AI: ESP32 Voice Assistant</h3>
      <p class="meta">2026 · Independent project</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>Built a desktop voice assistant around an ESP32-C3 with an INMP441 I²S microphone, a MAX98357A amplifier and speaker, a 1.3 inch LCD, a humidity sensor, an on/off switch and two buttons that scroll through pages (Wi-Fi, weather, room, Spotify).</li>
      <li>Implemented push-to-talk: a short press scrolls pages, a long press records audio and sends it over Wi-Fi to a Python Flask server on a laptop, which uses the OpenAI API for speech-to-text, chat replies and text-to-speech streamed back as 24 kHz PCM.</li>
      <li>Added live weather answers in English and Turkish by detecting weather questions and cities and pulling current data from the Open-Meteo API.</li>
      <li>Integrated Spotify through the Spotify Web API with OAuth tokens from the Spotify developer dashboard, so voice commands (play, pause, next, previous, resume) control Spotify on a phone.</li>
      <li>Keeps conversation memory across requests and published the firmware and server as open source. Source code: <a href="deskbuddy/OpenSource.ino">ESP32 firmware</a>, <a href="deskbuddy/server.py">laptop server</a> and <a href="deskbuddy/README.md">setup guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="diagram">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 910" width="1100" height="910" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block" role="img" aria-labelledby="wt wd">
<title id="wt">DeskBuddy AI wiring diagram</title>
<desc id="wd">An ESP32-C3 board connects to an INMP441 microphone board and a MAX98357A amplifier board over shared I2S clock lines, to a 1.3 inch OLED display and a humidity sensor board over I2C, to two push buttons on GPIO 4 and 5, and to 5 volts through an on/off switch. The amplifier drives a speaker.</desc>
